  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Aura</strong> faint Divination; <strong>CL</strong> 2nd<br>\n<strong>Slot</strong> any; <strong>Price</strong> 1,600 gp; <strong>Weight</strong> 0.5 lbs.</p>\n<p>Instilled with a suspiciously high amount of luck, these charms are often made with simple materials and prayed over by people who care for the individual it is being made for. Once per day, as a free action that can be taken even when it is not your turn, you may add 1d4 to one attack roll, skill check, saving throw, ability check (including Initiative rolls), or combat maneuver roll you are about to make. As an immediate action, you may instead grant this effect to an ally who can see and hear you. You may only use this effect once per roll and must do so before rolling the dice.</p>\n<p><strong>Flask Shard Effect:</strong> Increase the caster level of this item to the next increment of 5, add a +1 bonus to the result of the roll, and increase the number of daily uses by 1. Also, once per day for each flask shard used on this item, the user can meditate for one minute with this item to regain all daily uses of its effect. (This means a +1 lucky charm has a real maximum of 4 uses/day, a +2 has a real maximum of 9 uses/day, etc.) <strong>Flask Shard Limit:</strong> +4</p>\n<p><strong>Construction Requirements</strong><br>\nCraft Marvelous Item, Divination sphere (Divine Future); <strong>Cost</strong> 800 gp</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/marvelous-items#toc49\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
